@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 {
   "schema": 1,
   "source-sha256": "cf0761b2969ab7be03474449aac96da92374ba5c4c826d3aab808959d4f30565",
-  "replacement": "(def ^:private quote-string\n  (fn [s]\n    (let [buffer (BootstrapPrinterStringBuffer. nil)\n          length (.-length s)]\n      (.append buffer \"\\\"\")\n      (loop [i 0 start 0]\n        (if (< i length)\n          (let [unit (suss.bootstrap/string-slice s i (inc i))\n                escaped (get char-escapes unit)]\n            (if escaped\n              (do\n                (if (< start i)\n                  (.append buffer (suss.bootstrap/string-slice s start i))\n                  nil)\n                (.append buffer escaped)\n                (recur (inc i) (inc i)))\n              (recur (inc i) start)))\n          (do\n            (if (< start length)\n              (.append buffer (suss.bootstrap/string-slice s start length))\n              nil)\n            (.append buffer \"\\\"\")\n            (.toString buffer)))))))",
-  "rationale": "Retain private visibility and the single pinned signature. Replace the global seven-character JavaScript regex replacement with ordered UTF-16 code-unit traversal and the complete pinned escape table. Surround the result with the same quote characters; preserve every other code unit including unpaired surrogates without UTF-8 conversion. This is a string-storage adaptation, not an implementation of public regexp interoperability. Accumulate unchanged runs and escaped units in the printer-only immutable chunk buffer, then join once. Each input unit is examined once, and each run is copied once; no growing-prefix concatenation remains. Keep the complete escape table and preserve UTF-16 units, including unpaired surrogates."
+  "replacement": "(def ^:private quote-string\n  (fn [s]\n    (let [buffer (BootstrapPrinterStringBuffer. nil)\n          length (.-length s)]\n      (.append buffer \"\\\"\")\n      (loop [i 0 start 0]\n        (if (< i length)\n          (let [end (inc i)\n                unit (suss.bootstrap/string-slice s i end)\n                escaped (get char-escapes unit)]\n            (if escaped\n              (do\n                (if (< start i)\n                  (.append buffer (suss.bootstrap/string-slice s start i))\n                  nil)\n                (.append buffer escaped)\n                (recur end end))\n              (recur end start)))\n          (do\n            (if (< start length)\n              (.append buffer (suss.bootstrap/string-slice s start length))\n              nil)\n            (.append buffer \"\\\"\")\n            (.toString buffer)))))))",
+  "rationale": "Retain private visibility and the single pinned signature. Replace the global seven-character JavaScript regex replacement with ordered UTF-16 code-unit traversal and the complete pinned escape table. Surround the result with the same quote characters; preserve every other code unit including unpaired surrogates without UTF-8 conversion. This is a string-storage adaptation, not an implementation of public regexp interoperability. Accumulate unchanged runs and escaped units in the printer-only immutable chunk buffer, then join once. Each input unit is examined once, and each run is copied once; no growing-prefix concatenation remains. Keep the complete escape table and preserve UTF-16 units, including unpaired surrogates. Compute the next UTF-16 index once per reached input unit and reuse it for slicing and both recurrence positions. This removes repeated checked integer increments while keeping the same traversal, escape-table lookup, ordered buffer writes and final join. The existing long-string regression retains its100M operation-fuel limit."
 }
